#
# READING.
# - There is NO ~25 Mbit/s ceiling. Short probes understate by ramp (24.5 → 87.0 for
#   one stream). The earlier "RuggedFox uplink is the cap" finding stands on its own.
# - The path tops out near 100 Mbit/s: 99.3 aggregate with four streams vs 87.0 with
#   one (+14% for 4×). Per-stream flow control (noq-proto default stream_receive_window
#   1,250,000 B; nothing set in commonwealth-transport/src/iroh.rs:236-272) is NOT
#   falsified — with RTT only bounded above (≤160-280 ms) it permits ≥ 62 Mbit/s and
#   would predict 87 at ~115 ms — but it is not what bounds four streams. Between the
#   link (550-680 up, 186 down) and the path (~100) the gap is OURS: iroh/noq path
#   (Cubic default, 1200 B MTU, GSO falling back on EINVAL) or the relay-assisted
#   direct path. NEXT INSTRUMENT: print Connection::rtt beside the path line
#   (iroh-1.0.2/src/endpoint/connection.rs:1016) so the window arithmetic closes, and
#   compare a plain TCP pull on the same pair.
# - THE FINDING: the path DEGRADES WITH DURATION — 87.0 over 25 s, 55.2 over 623 s
#   with 3 reconnects and four >1 s gaps. A player experiences 87 for a while and
#   then seconds of nothing. That is a stability question no mean-rate bar surfaces,
#   and it is the one a shim author will hit first.
# VM cost: $0.215/h × 34 min (20:51-21:25 UTC) ≈ $0.12; destroyed after these readings, none listed after.
